The conditionality of the recommendation to deploy spatial repellents is based on the GDG’s judgement that the balance of desirable and undesirable effects probably favours deployment alongside ITNs or IRS, but considers that the systematic review found considerable heterogeneity in protective effect, largely explained by different levels of coverage achieved with the spatial repellent in each trial. The GDG therefore noted that effective protection of the population with spatial repellents depends on continuous high coverage in the target area, with duration of efficacy of the product and distribution model being the key determinants of feasibility and cost-effectiveness.

